      "writtenOn": "2026-11-21T01:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The description of the hack is incorrect: we don\u0027t create a new web injector at all here.\n\nWhat we want to do is to have access to the `DynamicSet\u003cWebloginListener\u003e` without having direct access to the `WebInjector` because it wasn\u0027t shared with us.\n\nIdeally, we should have this exposed at the Gerrit level by the Daemon with a simple `getWebInjector()`, but that method doesn\u0027t exist in Gerrit v3.13.\n\nWhat we do instead is a hack to get hold of the `DynamicSet\u003cWebLoginListener\u003e` by simulating the creation of a sort of _ad hoc_ plugin that contains the dynamic items of Gerrit\u0027s web injector and is named `componentName`.\n\nThen we use the new injector to extract the `DynamicSet\u003cWebLoginListener\u003e` and add the \u0027 RedirectAdminsToBslUrl \u0027 class artificially to the set associated with the _ad hoc_ plugin named `componentName`.\n\nThis should be flagged as a `TODO` to be sanitised in master by introducing a simple `Daemon.getWebInjector()` method, which would make this whole hack redundant.\n\nIt would be better to do something more radical by extracting this hack into a separate class that adds this dynamic item to the web injector, so that the hacky stuff is confined and well identified.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 94
      },
